0e5b745d-a94f-4492-ba2b-3a18dfdc1d27	ea29dc13-86fe-4153-9d4e-55efd083d751	polite ending particles (f)	\N	<p>\r\n  <a href="tts:นะ">นะ</a> /na/ – a softening particle used to add friendliness, encouragement, or politeness to a statement<br>\r\n  <a href="tts:คะ">คะ</a> /kha/ – usually used at the end of <strong>questions</strong> and <strong>requests</strong>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>\r\nWhen used together at the end of a sentence it softens the tone and makes speech sound friendlier, more gentle and non-harsh. It can be used with requests, suggestions, statements, questions, and corrections. It adds warmth and politeness, similar to saying “okay?”, “alright?”, or simply softening the mood of the sentence.\r\n</p>	2	2026-07-12 00:18:03.739518+00	2026-10-23 19:13:40.806561+00	t
